A||||10||Terrybogin||Headlight Motor Blues. . .||||8
Z||000000||Terrybogin||10-12-1999||10:25 PM||||I finally got my 85 SE back after my brother has had it for about 6 weeks. Now the pass. side headlight motor keeps running after the light gets up or down. I had to disconnect it to make it stop running. Did the relay stick or gears strip or what???? Can it be fixed or should I shop for another motor? HELP!!!!!||||reg||8
Z||000001||87FieroGT||10-12-1999||10:39 PM||||Since your car is an 85' it would more than likely be the plastic gear that has been stripped do to the grease inside getting gummed up. The cheapest thing would be to find someone on the web who makes and sells a metal replacement gear or find a good motor in a parts yard. The best and most expensive thing would be to by a new one that would have a warranty on it. Good luck in whatever you decide to do.||||reg||12
Z||000002||HotFieroGT||10-13-1999||12:11 AM||||I don't know if the 85 is the same as the 88 but I had problems with mine also.  After having a heart attack after pricing a new ones.  I took the motors apart and there was a pile of plastic dust inside.  I tried new plastic dowels, that didn't work.  I then tried aluminum ones and haven't had a problem since.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||10-13-1999||03:36 AM||||I was informed that Alan Mooty sold bronze gears to replace the white plastic ones.  I dont have the phone number offhand, but I called him and he told me 45 bucks for the gear.  He also said he had to machine up some more, but I sent him the 45 anyways, and I never got the gear and it has been well over a month now.  I dont know what the deal is , but i sent him a letter inquiring on the status.<BR>Alan Mooty<BR>8061 Nicklaus Dr<BR>Orlando FL 32825||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||10-13-1999||09:09 AM||||Ecklers Corvettes here in Titusville,FL offers the gears in Plastic and Bronze.  I bought Plastic Gears for about $21 each and used some decent grease.  I figure that if the original plastic gears lasted 15 years, the new ones should too.  <P>BTW, you would want to ask for the Headlight gear for an 85 Vette.....<P> <A HREF="http://www.ecklers.com" TARGET=_blank>www.ecklers.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||88 Fiero||10-13-1999||10:38 AM||||Since you guys are talking about rebuilding your headlight motor. Here is another guy that sells the headlight motor in both alloy or steel gear. It's a little more money, but I think it's worth it.<P>1987 to 1988 -- $50.00<BR>1984 to 1986 -- $65.00<P>Chris Cook<BR>(317) 786-9418<BR>cook6090@cris.com<P>He also sells the Replacement Fiero GT Quarter Windows for $75.00 a side.<BR>I hope this helps....{=o)||||reg||1
Z||000006||TOM||10-13-1999||10:58 AM||||On the early year motors its not the grease that causes the problems. Its the drive damper inside the gear. It crumbles after it gets old then binds the gears and causes it to strip. I sell replacement gears and rebuilt motors.||||reg||1
Z||000007||AL||10-14-1999||12:57 AM||||ok my motors don't do a thing, is there a way to test if the motors are good?if i take the motors out of the car can i test them if i hook them up to a battery or what? give me ideas guys. bye the way my car is an 86.5 gt.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Carrolles||10-14-1999||04:43 PM||||If it is an 85 you can probably salvage the gears you have.  In operation the gear traveles less than 180 degrees.  If it is stripped it is probably only affected at a small part of the gear.  You can carefully take the gear out (do not move anything while the gear is out) and turn it around 180 degrees and put it back in with the unstripped teeth in operation now.<BR>Give it a try.||||reg||1
Z||000009||tiacPaul||10-15-1999||12:10 AM||||One of the headlight motors on my 84 doesn't work at all. The other doesn't stop when going up or down. Any ideas on why it isn't stopping?||||reg||4
Z||000010||Greg Piet||10-15-1999||02:43 AM||||The following site has a detailed section on troubleshooting your headlight motors. <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/osg.html#diag" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/osg.html#diag</A> ||||reg||1
